!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/link/valid/a-payload-of-the-kernels-constructor-completes-the-documents-own-incomplete-entry-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/link-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §3.3, [TSON-SCHEMA] §3.4.1 (the wait order, proposed), [TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.5"
  description: """
    A construction's payload is read in the namespace of the schema that writes it, its own entries included. `rows`
    is an incomplete entry, and `!rows { … }` in the kernel's `meta.record` payload completes it wherever a type is
    written in place: a field's type, and an element type in place inside another construction. `post` is written
    first: its payload names `rows` and waits on it being ready.
    """
  valid: {
    binds: [post]
  }
}
